# tests/vars/startset.rxt -- [START-SET] stage 2 (D148): sabotage S500's
# answer witness. A variable reads as "every byte, nullable" in the start-set
# walk (src/facts/startset.c), so `${v}x` is not a VM-hat mover; a walk whose
# A_VAR arm dropped its bytes would make it one, and the seek, finding no
# start byte, would skip every match. Verified by verify_vars.py (this
# directory's oracle: the value quotemeta-spliced, asked of libpcre2).

pattern ${v}x
features vars
var v "a"
m "ax" 0 2
m "zzax" 2 4
m "xax" 1 3
n "x"
n "a"
